    "raw_public_english_response": "The proposal was submitted and accepted with a valid normalization receipt (no conflicting explicit settings, no normalization applied).\n\n**Assessment summary for case `gaussian-b3lyp-explicit-d4-unsupported`:**\n\n| Setting | Requested | Registry status | Outcome |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Functional | B3LYP | `exact_registered` (`gaussian.functional.b3lyp`) | Accepted, preserved |\n| Basis | def2-SVP | `exact_registered` (`gaussian.basis.bse.def2svp`) | Accepted, preserved |\n| Dispersion | D4 | `unknown_unverified` (`scientific_settings.unknown_unverified`); dispersion inventory is a `coverage_gap` (0 entries) for gaussian | **Blocker** |\n\n**Readiness:** `blocked_unverified_setting`, with `scientific_settings.unknown_unverified` recorded as the blocking rule.\n\nKey points:\n- The explicit `D4` literal was **preserved, not silently dropped or substituted** (e.g., not rewritten to D3), per the request constraint.\n- Gaussian 16.C01 has no native separate D4 correction, and the registry exposes no exact match for the D4 dispersion literal — the deterministic blocker is the unverified D4 setting.\n- Evidence ceiling is `loader_renderer_verification_only`; no engine execution, no scientific-adequacy verification was claimed.\n- No native input, no ChemSmart command, no project write, and no execution were authored or requested.\n\nSubmission receipt: `72c90e19b3ef79cd78cf37f98d5498e7b879f9c86f4b858ca0320c449f0812ed`.",
